# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/

# Godot regenerates these on import; keep only the source assets in git.
*.import

# Trinst prop/building textures under assets/trinst/{interiors,shapes}/:
#   * albedo *.jpg / *.png are RE-EXTRACTED from the committed .glb meshes on import,
#     so they stay ignored (regenerated on every machine).
#   * the algorithmically baked PBR maps (*_normal/_rough/_ao.png from
#     tools/enhance_materials.gd) are NOT regenerated by import. Ignoring those too
#     is exactly why a fresh clone (e.g. the Windows box) showed missing materials
#     and an invisible prefabs_tower1 while the Linux tree looked fine -- so the maps
#     are tracked now (the !negations below).
# Commit the maps from the machine that ran the bake:
#     git add minions-port/assets/trinst/interiors minions-port/assets/trinst/shapes
# (albedo stays ignored). Or skip all this and ship a single .exe -- see
# docs/BUILDING_WINDOWS_EXE.md, which bundles whatever is on disk.
/assets/trinst/interiors/*.jpg
/assets/trinst/interiors/*.png
!/assets/trinst/interiors/*_normal.png
!/assets/trinst/interiors/*_rough.png
!/assets/trinst/interiors/*_ao.png
/assets/trinst/shapes/*.jpg
/assets/trinst/shapes/*.png
!/assets/trinst/shapes/*_normal.png
!/assets/trinst/shapes/*_rough.png
!/assets/trinst/shapes/*_ao.png
